Experiment 1 — Lexical Analyzer with Symbol Table
Aim

To develop a lexical analyzer using FLEX to recognize tokens such as identifiers, constants, comments, and operators in a C program and to create a symbol table while recognizing identifiers.

Algorithm
Start the program.
Include the required header files.
Define regular expressions for:
Identifiers
Constants
Comments
Operators
Declare a symbol table containing identifier names and types.
Define FLEX rules to recognize each token.
When an identifier is recognized, search the symbol table.
If the identifier is not present, insert it into the symbol table.
Print the recognized tokens.
Open the input C file and call yylex().
Display the symbol table.
Stop.
Pseudocode
START

Initialize symbol table

Define patterns:
    Identifier
    Constant
    Comment
    Operator

Read input C program

WHILE input is not finished:
    Get next token

    IF token is Identifier:
        IF identifier is not in symbol table:
            Insert identifier
        Print "Identifier"

    ELSE IF token is Constant:
        Print "Constant"

    ELSE IF token is Comment:
        Print "Comment"

    ELSE IF token is Operator:
        Print "Operator"

    ELSE:
        Ignore token

END WHILE

Display symbol table

STOP
